WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.369
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Thursday, November fifth.

2
00:00:04.369 --> 00:00:07.216
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.216 --> 00:00:11.887
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:11.887 --> 00:00:13.435
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:13.435 --> 00:00:17.304
Another tanker was struck in the Arabian Gulf off northern Qatar.

6
00:00:17.304 --> 00:00:24.147
Iran's Revolutionary Guard again claims vessels caught fire near the Strait of Hormuz.

7
00:00:24.147 --> 00:00:29.050
And in Saudi Arabia, the Houthis claim they hit Riyadh's main airport, while cancellations continue.

8
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.601
Here's the detail.

9
00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:34.624
Gulf shipping.

10
00:00:34.624 --> 00:00:41.736
Confirmed by UK Maritime Trade Operations: late Wednesday, a tanker about fifty nautical miles north of Qatar was struck by two unidentified projectiles.

11
00:00:41.736 --> 00:00:47.855
Crew status, damage, and environmental impact were still unconfirmed when the warning was issued.

12
00:00:47.855 --> 00:00:55.881
That position is in the Arabian Gulf, which the latest joint maritime threat update, issued before this incident, rates substantial.

13
00:00:55.881 --> 00:00:58.697
The Strait of Hormuz remains assessed severe.

14
00:00:58.697 --> 00:01:07.234
Separately, Iran's Revolutionary Guard says two oil tankers and a tugboat caught fire after using unauthorised routes through the strait.

15
00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:08.923
That is a claim only.

16
00:01:08.923 --> 00:01:13.145
The vessels have not been identified in matching UKMTO warnings.

17
00:01:13.145 --> 00:01:17.766
Yesterday's claim of four tankers hit by mines also remains unmatched.

18
00:01:17.766 --> 00:01:28.340
Tueri suggests operators with Gulf voyages review routing against the current area assessments, and plan for continued attack risk without assuming any single claim is confirmed.

19
00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.799
Saudi Arabia.

20
00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:39.333
Claim only, reported by Yemen's Houthis: a ballistic missile strike on King Khalid International Airport in Riyadh on Wednesday, with claimed damage.

21
00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:41.988
Saudi authorities have not confirmed a hit.

22
00:01:41.988 --> 00:01:49.967
The US Mission security alert of November second still stands, warning of potential attacks on airports and possible flight disruption.

23
00:01:49.967 --> 00:01:51.577
It is not a new alert.

24
00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:59.114
At about two thirty-five p.m. local time today, Flightradar twenty-four showed about seventeen percent of Riyadh flights cancelled.

25
00:01:59.114 --> 00:02:04.053
Earlier snapshots used different bases, so no day-to-day trend can be drawn.

26
00:02:04.053 --> 00:02:11.529
Tueri suggests travelers keep flexible plans and confirm each flight with the airline before leaving for the airport.

27
00:02:11.529 --> 00:02:14.446
India.

28
00:02:14.446 --> 00:02:24.266
Confirmed by the India Meteorological Department: the remnant of Cyclone Murasu weakened further into a low pressure area over east Telangana and coastal Andhra Pradesh early Thursday.

29
00:02:24.266 --> 00:02:29.855
Rain continues, with isolated heavy rain still possible, but Wednesday's extremely heavy totals have eased.

30
00:02:29.855 --> 00:02:41.196
Tueri suggests organizations with people in the region continue to check flooding and road conditions before movement, and confirm staff welfare where disruption was heaviest.

31
00:02:41.196 --> 00:02:42.530
Operations check.

32
00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:47.841
Borders and health, US: the Ebola attestation rule remains in force for flights to the United States.

33
00:02:47.841 --> 00:02:51.626
No new change on the CDC page.

34
00:02:51.626 --> 00:02:52.649
No attestation, no boarding.

35
00:02:52.649 --> 00:03:07.599
Borders and health, Nigeria: an NCDC self-isolation guideline confirms twenty-one day self-quarantine and monitoring for returnees from Uganda and arrivals from countries with ongoing Ebola transmission, with Port Health screening on arrival.

36
00:03:07.599 --> 00:03:12.578
A blanket rule for every international arrival is still not confirmed with the authority.

37
00:03:12.578 --> 00:03:28.998
Borders and health, Madagascar: Britain's Foreign Office says Madagascar may refuse entry to people who have been in or transited the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Kenya, or Nigeria in the last twenty-one days, with limited exceptions who must complete paid quarantine.

38
00:03:28.998 --> 00:03:36.501
Borders and health, Ghana: FCDO says additional Ebola screening and a health declaration are in place at entry points.

39
00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:45.377
Aviation: European flights again faced bomb-threat diversions and disruptions Thursday, including a Dublin to Rome flight diverted in France; no devices confirmed in reporting we reviewed.

40
00:03:45.377 --> 00:03:53.594
Infrastructure: Russian strikes continue to disrupt Ukrainian power and connectivity; no new Zhytomyr measurement this cycle.

41
00:03:53.594 --> 00:03:59.988
Hazards: Mayon volcano remains at alert level three, reported via Philippine media.

42
00:03:59.988 --> 00:04:11.516
Belize: Canada's travel advice still describes a thirty-day state of emergency declared October thirty-first in parts of Belize City and nearby areas; Britain's Foreign Office page has not yet reflected that emergency.

43
00:04:11.516 --> 00:04:15.330
That's today's brief.

44
00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:16.817
Current as of six a.m.

45
00:04:16.817 --> 00:04:18.849
Central, Thursday.

46
00:04:18.849 --> 00:04:19.706
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

47
00:04:19.706 --> 00:04:26.591
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

48
00:04:26.591 --> 00:04:28.993
Check the original source before you act.

49
00:04:28.993 --> 00:04:38.005
Tueri Systems provides information verification, communications support, and operational decision support for organizations working in changing conditions.

50
00:04:38.005 --> 00:04:40.704
Learn more at tuerisystems.com.

51
00:04:40.704 --> 00:04:41.942
Thanks for listening.
